WEBVTT

00:01.501 --> 00:05.296
There are likely no Titans among
the recruits of the 104th Cadet Corps!

00:06.548 --> 00:08.758
Multiple Titans from the south!

00:09.884 --> 00:12.303
Wall Rose has been breached!

00:17.642 --> 00:21.730
The 104th Cadet Corps were kept isolated

00:21.938 --> 00:23.940
under the suspicion
of having Titans within their ranks.

00:25.608 --> 00:28.319
But with the sudden appearance of Titans,

00:28.987 --> 00:31.698
couriers were sent out
to warn each district.

00:35.452 --> 00:36.703
As you may know,

00:37.162 --> 00:39.914
today marks the darkest day
in humanity's history!

00:40.498 --> 00:44.252
If ever there is a time
that humanity needed to give its all,

00:44.502 --> 00:45.670
that time is now!

00:46.629 --> 00:47.589
However...

00:52.802 --> 00:53.720
What?

00:54.054 --> 00:55.388
They all started sprinting!

00:58.266 --> 01:01.311
The cause of this crisis
remains in the dark.

01:02.687 --> 01:04.647
For now, no one still knows.

01:12.989 --> 01:16.951
I must say, what a clever idea.

03:00.430 --> 03:02.849
TROST DISTRICT

03:02.974 --> 03:03.933
Commander Pyxis!

03:05.101 --> 03:06.394
Titans have been spotted!

03:07.228 --> 03:09.981
Wall Rose has been breached!

03:13.443 --> 03:16.821
STOHESS DISTRICT

03:18.489 --> 03:22.201
What the hell does all this mean?

03:22.744 --> 03:25.246
-Damn it!
-But...

03:27.165 --> 03:30.376
would Titans break walls
with Titans in it?

03:31.419 --> 03:35.173
It happened before.
They busted the wall to get into our city.

03:35.840 --> 03:37.133
That was a gate.

03:39.427 --> 03:41.804
Armin? What are you saying?

03:42.388 --> 03:43.681
The thing about the walls...

03:44.474 --> 03:48.853
There are no gaps between rocks
or any indications of cracks.

03:49.270 --> 03:51.731
We can't tell how they're made.

03:54.150 --> 03:57.195
So, what if they're made
of hardened Titan skin?

03:59.948 --> 04:01.783
It must be pretty versatile

04:01.866 --> 04:03.826
if Annie can make
a barrier around herself.

04:06.371 --> 04:09.082
Titans in the wall...

04:10.792 --> 04:12.794
Section Commander! What are you doing?

04:13.670 --> 04:15.588
We're supposed to leave in five minutes!

04:15.922 --> 04:19.217
-Please hurry up!
-There's something I need to confirm...

04:23.179 --> 04:24.138
Hey.

04:24.764 --> 04:27.141
-Get moving.
-Oh, sorry!

04:27.600 --> 04:30.603
-What about him?
-He's been ready for a while now.

04:39.612 --> 04:42.657
Eren, wear it properly.
It's cold at night.

04:43.449 --> 04:44.492
Sorry to keep you waiting!

04:45.827 --> 04:48.204
It took longer to prepare than we thought.

04:54.127 --> 04:55.003
Well...

04:55.753 --> 04:58.339
Isn't this a priest
from the Order of the Walls?

04:58.756 --> 05:01.676
Yes, Nick and I are the best of buddies.

05:01.759 --> 05:02.885
Right?

05:03.511 --> 05:05.013
Don't let him bother you.

05:05.722 --> 05:08.933
The whole make-up of this squad
doesn't make any sense.

05:09.309 --> 05:10.560
Does it, Levi?

05:11.227 --> 05:13.062
No, I think it might.

05:13.855 --> 05:16.274
Erwin picked them out for a reason.

05:17.150 --> 05:18.359
Open the gate!

05:27.076 --> 05:29.537
The situation within Wall Rose is unclear.

05:30.163 --> 05:32.373
But everything until Ehrmich is safe.

05:32.707 --> 05:34.375
We'll save time going through there.

05:35.084 --> 05:36.878
-Move out!
-Yes, sir!

05:38.755 --> 05:40.506
-Bring us out.
-Yes, sir!

05:55.813 --> 06:00.651
This whole time, Titans have been
protecting us from Titans.

06:12.705 --> 06:14.248
What? Did he know?

06:14.874 --> 06:18.544
There are Titans inside the walls
and he already knows about it?

06:19.253 --> 06:20.797
Yes, however...

06:21.672 --> 06:24.258
he's kept his mouth shut this entire time.

06:26.594 --> 06:28.513
But now he's coming with us

06:29.305 --> 06:30.848
to witness the harsh reality.

06:31.265 --> 06:34.602
Will his beliefs remain strong enough
for him to stay silent?

06:35.186 --> 06:38.648
Or will seeing it with his own eyes
make him question himself?

06:40.108 --> 06:42.985
No! This is all backward!

06:43.277 --> 06:45.988
If there's something you know, tell us!

06:46.364 --> 06:50.368
Nothing's more important than
preventing humans from going extinct!

06:50.952 --> 06:53.079
Eren, settle down.

06:53.496 --> 06:55.123
You're still not fully healed.

06:56.707 --> 06:58.960
There's more than one way to get answers.

07:00.169 --> 07:02.463
I may be injured and useless right now,

07:03.339 --> 07:05.716
but it doesn't take much to watch one man.

07:06.425 --> 07:10.972
I'm hoping we can settle this
without blasting a hole through anyone.

07:11.597 --> 07:12.598
Aren't you?

07:12.807 --> 07:16.227
Threatening him won't work, Levi.
Believe me, I've tried.

07:17.145 --> 07:21.232
It seems to me that this priest
is capable of sound judgment.

07:22.483 --> 07:23.901
That's why I wonder...

07:24.819 --> 07:26.612
What if the reason he won't talk

07:27.071 --> 07:30.741
is that he knows something
more important than the fate of humanity?

07:34.454 --> 07:37.623
-See that? It's the village!
-Is that the last one?

07:38.082 --> 07:41.586
No! My village is deep in the forest!

07:42.837 --> 07:44.505
I'll go there alone!

07:45.214 --> 07:46.048
All right!

07:46.424 --> 07:48.342
Leave this village to me!

07:48.676 --> 07:49.510
Got it!

07:56.476 --> 07:58.478
Hey, Sasha, stop it!

07:59.187 --> 08:02.482
Sasha, you've been stealing snacks again?

08:02.857 --> 08:05.693
Stop! Spit it out!
Get it out of your mouth!

08:05.818 --> 08:09.363
We plan to smoke that for winter,
you moron!

08:19.582 --> 08:21.626
You dumb girl!

08:22.543 --> 08:23.419
Fine!

08:24.045 --> 08:25.338
Have it your way.

08:27.423 --> 08:28.466
Goddamn it.

08:38.726 --> 08:40.603
Sasha, have you asked yourself

08:41.521 --> 08:44.524
why the world is changing?

08:45.608 --> 08:47.151
Why the game is more difficult to find?

08:47.318 --> 08:49.904
And why the forest has been shrinking
these past few years?

08:50.238 --> 08:51.614
Have you ever thought about it?

08:54.200 --> 08:58.287
It's because more people are coming
and taking food from the forest.

08:59.080 --> 09:00.248
That's why I'm hungry.

09:01.624 --> 09:02.917
That's true.

09:04.252 --> 09:05.169
But, hey...

09:05.586 --> 09:08.047
They lost their homes
and had no place to go.

09:08.506 --> 09:10.675
They had no other option.

09:11.217 --> 09:14.887
Losing it was their fault.
They should leave ours.

09:16.847 --> 09:18.307
Titans took it from them.

09:18.641 --> 09:21.060
They knocked a hole
straight through Wall Maria.

09:21.602 --> 09:23.187
Where else can they go?

09:24.855 --> 09:28.025
You can feed a hell of a lot more people

09:28.276 --> 09:31.404
by clearing the forest and planting grain.

09:34.532 --> 09:36.909
Maybe it's time for our family
to let go of the forest

09:37.451 --> 09:39.662
and give up hunting for good.

09:41.539 --> 09:45.001
Every horse that we raise
is money in our pockets.

09:45.293 --> 09:46.961
The government said they would pay us.

09:47.044 --> 09:48.796
You've got to be kidding!

09:48.921 --> 09:51.757
If we give up hunting,
we'll be giving up who we are!

09:51.841 --> 09:55.970
Why should we give a damn about the people
who make fun of our lifestyle?

09:56.262 --> 09:57.221
I'll tell you why.

09:59.223 --> 10:03.311
It's because we're all part
of the same world.

10:04.020 --> 10:07.732
We humans,
we've always been a pack of animals.

10:08.399 --> 10:10.818
Sure, we all live in different ways.

10:11.068 --> 10:13.195
But when the space is this small,

10:13.529 --> 10:16.657
we have to join the group
and do what's best to--

10:16.741 --> 10:18.367
No! I refuse!

10:18.784 --> 10:22.955
We've lived here all our lives,
just like the way our ancestors taught us!

10:23.205 --> 10:25.583
We owe nothing to those outsiders!

10:30.796 --> 10:33.674
I see. So be it.

10:36.218 --> 10:38.429
You can live here in this forest,

10:38.721 --> 10:41.724
along with the others who think the same.

10:43.476 --> 10:44.977
But, Sasha...

10:45.436 --> 10:48.272
are you willing to die for that choice?

10:49.732 --> 10:52.026
No matter what trouble comes your way,

10:52.234 --> 10:54.070
you can't go begging for help.

10:54.904 --> 10:56.364
If you're not there for them,

10:56.906 --> 11:00.284
don't expect them to be there for you.

11:01.869 --> 11:03.746
I'm willing to give up our traditions

11:03.996 --> 11:06.165
if it means I can live with my family.

11:07.083 --> 11:09.168
That goes to show you
our world is connected,

11:09.335 --> 11:11.003
whether you like it or not.

11:13.297 --> 11:17.134
Sasha, are you that much of a scaredy-cat?

11:18.302 --> 11:21.263
Is it that hard for you
to leave this forest behind

11:21.889 --> 11:24.600
and get along with others?

11:28.854 --> 11:31.482
It's been three years
since I've been back.

11:31.816 --> 11:34.819
Surely he realized something was amiss
and fled...

11:39.323 --> 11:41.867
It can't be! Way out here?

11:45.121 --> 11:47.706
They've already come this far?

11:49.667 --> 11:53.129
This place isn't safe for people anymore.

11:57.550 --> 11:58.551
What's that?

11:59.260 --> 12:00.886
A new village?

13:17.838 --> 13:21.342
Damn! If I don't slice it off,
it will just heal itself!

13:30.809 --> 13:31.936
A child?

13:41.070 --> 13:42.863
I'm so sorry.

13:57.836 --> 13:59.213
What's your name?

14:02.925 --> 14:05.886
-Don't worry. It will be okay.
-What will?

14:06.011 --> 14:08.847
What? I mean...

14:10.349 --> 14:12.184
Steady.

14:12.518 --> 14:13.978
Well, you see...

14:16.689 --> 14:18.399
You're kidding me! Hey!

14:18.732 --> 14:20.484
Please wait for us!

14:23.153 --> 14:26.740
There's no need to worry.
Please stay calm. It will come right back.

14:26.907 --> 14:28.868
Why are you so nice when you talk?

14:29.159 --> 14:29.994
What?

14:39.336 --> 14:40.421
Run away from here!

14:43.924 --> 14:45.175
It'll be okay!

14:46.677 --> 14:49.179
Why? Everyone already left.

14:50.389 --> 14:53.893
The whole village knew
my mother's legs were bad.

14:54.768 --> 14:57.313
But not a single person came to help.

14:57.730 --> 14:59.356
All I could do was watch.

15:19.168 --> 15:20.461
It'll be okay!

15:24.173 --> 15:25.132
It's okay.

15:28.761 --> 15:31.472
-You're starting to tick me off.
-What?

15:32.139 --> 15:35.017
That stupid way
you talk politely to everyone.

15:36.852 --> 15:39.396
Why don't you talk to other cadets
like normal?

15:39.813 --> 15:42.274
Well, you see...

15:43.943 --> 15:46.278
Wait. Let me guess.

15:46.487 --> 15:49.740
You're embarrassed by the way
people from your village sound.

15:50.074 --> 15:54.578
Bullseye? I'm surprised
an idiot like you cares so much.

15:55.037 --> 15:57.373
You can't do anything but hunt,

15:57.498 --> 15:59.500
and to top it off,
you're afraid of people.

16:01.126 --> 16:04.505
I bet you don't have a single good reason
for aiming to become a soldier.

16:05.005 --> 16:07.383
-Your parents probably--
-Stop it, Ymir! You're being--

16:07.549 --> 16:08.592
Sasha!

16:08.717 --> 16:10.719
Are you going to care
what other people think

16:10.844 --> 16:12.846
and be someone you're not your whole life?

16:12.972 --> 16:14.765
What a pile of shit.

16:14.848 --> 16:16.934
You're fine as is,
so talk in your own words,

16:17.101 --> 16:18.769
for crying out loud.

16:21.146 --> 16:23.524
Thank you...

16:24.608 --> 16:25.818
very much.

16:26.151 --> 16:28.612
-What?
-I'm sorry.

16:29.029 --> 16:30.489
I'm not yet...

16:30.572 --> 16:31.907
Cut it out!

16:32.533 --> 16:35.744
There's nothing wrong
with the way she talks!

16:37.663 --> 16:39.748
Sasha is who Sasha wants to be.

16:40.249 --> 16:42.001
Her words will always be her own.

16:43.002 --> 16:44.420
And I happen to like her.

16:46.463 --> 16:48.007
Have it your way.

16:48.424 --> 16:51.301
Even if she changed the way she talked,

16:51.427 --> 16:53.429
it won't change the fact
that she's annoying.

16:53.637 --> 16:57.266
You know, not everyone
is as insensitive as you.

16:57.516 --> 16:58.684
Excuse me?

16:59.143 --> 17:00.060
You little...

17:03.063 --> 17:05.566
Hey! What are you laughing at?

17:06.108 --> 17:07.943
Oh, I'm sorry!

17:14.825 --> 17:17.745
Of all times, why am I now remembering

17:18.287 --> 17:20.664
the silly, pointless days in the past?

17:21.206 --> 17:24.376
They're all I can think of.

17:27.296 --> 17:28.630
Hey, listen up.

17:30.090 --> 17:32.926
You'll be fine. Keep following this path.

17:33.635 --> 17:35.012
Run as far as you can.

17:35.721 --> 17:38.640
I promise someone will be there
to help you.

17:38.932 --> 17:40.851
You might not find them right away.

17:41.560 --> 17:44.104
But still, keep running until you do!

17:45.105 --> 17:46.190
Now, go!

17:46.815 --> 17:47.816
Run!

17:51.820 --> 17:53.405
Get running!

18:09.713 --> 18:13.175
If I take out both eyes,
it'll buy us plenty of time.

18:19.848 --> 18:21.433
Only two left.

18:23.143 --> 18:24.269
Relax...

18:24.603 --> 18:27.064
It's just a big...

18:27.648 --> 18:29.817
slow-moving target!

18:33.237 --> 18:34.154
Got it!

18:38.075 --> 18:39.243
One more arrow.

18:39.827 --> 18:42.496
But, if I miss this...

18:46.166 --> 18:47.543
we can't escape.

18:48.210 --> 18:50.671
If I miss, me and...

18:51.713 --> 18:52.673
that girl...

19:20.951 --> 19:22.619
I slipped out thanks to that blood.

19:23.662 --> 19:24.997
Now I've got to find that girl!

19:31.295 --> 19:33.130
What? Sasha?

19:49.188 --> 19:52.816
We have been giving horses
to everyone in the area.

19:53.150 --> 19:56.153
That girl told us
someone was still back there.

19:57.362 --> 19:59.740
Who would have thought it was you?

20:00.782 --> 20:03.619
You fought off a Titan for that girl,
didn't you?

20:06.872 --> 20:09.082
Sasha, you're all I hoped for.

20:11.877 --> 20:12.794
Father...

20:15.714 --> 20:16.548
I'm home.

20:21.136 --> 20:22.179
Conny, wait!

20:23.180 --> 20:24.264
Calm down!

20:24.598 --> 20:26.558
There could be Titans anywhere!

20:27.142 --> 20:28.769
Get back here, Conny!

20:32.272 --> 20:33.106
This can't be...

20:38.445 --> 20:41.448
Anyone? Is anyone there?

20:43.450 --> 20:45.244
It's me! Conny!

20:45.619 --> 20:47.663
I came back!

20:57.172 --> 20:58.131
My house!

21:02.010 --> 21:02.970
Dad...

21:03.887 --> 21:04.763
Mom...

21:05.222 --> 21:07.266
Sunny, Martin!

21:08.267 --> 21:10.143
Please be okay!

21:26.243 --> 21:28.036
Conny! Get back!

21:28.954 --> 21:29.913
It's...

21:30.414 --> 21:31.373
my house.

21:32.332 --> 21:33.208
My...

21:34.001 --> 21:34.876
Conny...

21:35.711 --> 21:36.920
Fall back, you two!

21:37.337 --> 21:38.672
I'll scout the area!

21:41.925 --> 21:43.593
Wait, it's...

21:44.386 --> 21:47.097
-It can't move?
-Not with those legs.

21:50.183 --> 21:52.102
Then how?

21:53.186 --> 21:54.980
How did it even get here?

23:29.574 --> 23:31.743
"I'm sure my family is safe and sound."

23:32.661 --> 23:36.498
Shaking off the dread of Titans
appearing in his hometown,

23:36.998 --> 23:39.209
Conny once again departs.

23:40.085 --> 23:42.129
Battle erupts across the lands

23:42.420 --> 23:44.673
while the mystery of the Titans remains.

23:45.674 --> 23:47.634
As the situation worsens,

23:48.301 --> 23:50.303
Eren and company,
who are heading for Ehrmich District,

23:50.512 --> 23:52.722
receive a clue
that might reveal the truth.

23:53.890 --> 23:57.144
Next episode, "Southwestward."
